From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepOffset_MakeLoops orients the splits of a
 cap against the offset faces

BRepOffset_MakeLoops::BuildOnContext rebuilds each cap, the face that closes the opening left by a
removed face, by splitting it with BRepAlgo_Loop on the reversed face and registering the splits
(Loops.NewFaces()) as the images of the cap. The splits come back oriented as BRepAlgo_Loop built
them, with no regard to the offset faces they meet along the cut edges.

BRepOffset_MakeOffset::MakeShells then hands the roots of myImageOffset to BRepTools_Quilt, which
sews them in the order it is given them and keeps the orientation of the first face of each
connected component as the orientation of the component. A cap split that runs the same way as the
offset faces along their shared edges is the odd one out, so a shell whose first root is a cap
split comes out inside out. Which root is first is decided by the root order, so the result
depended on it: before 0053 on the heap (hash order of the TShape addresses), after 0053 on the
binding order, which for a block with a blind hole whose floor is removed puts the cap first, so
a defect that appeared in a fraction of builds appeared in all of them.

Reproducer (57.5 x 40 x 27.5 box, two d1.5 holes 40 deep along X, BRepOffsetAPI_MakeThickSolid
::MakeThickSolidByJoin removing the floor of the second hole, offset -1.95, tolerance 1e-3,
GeomAbs_Arc, 200 fresh copies of the block): 21 invalid on upstream IR with the roots in heap
order, 200 of 200 invalid with the roots in binding order (0053 alone), 0 of 200 with this change,
volume 19219.48 in every one (the upstream figures, measured on upstream IR; the package-side
measurement is below).

The change records, for every offset face that borders the cap, the orientation of the edges of
its last images (BRepAlgo_Image::LastImage), and reverses a split of the cap whose edges shared
with those faces run the same way in it as in them. Edges that occur more than once in the split
(seams) and edges the split does not share with an offset face are not counted. A split that
shares no edge is left as it is. Nothing else in BuildOnContext changes.

Measured on macOS arm64 by linking the patched BRepOffset_MakeLoops.cxx object into a copy of the
v4.0.0-kernel.6 asset (which carries 0053): a Swift test builds the block above afresh 100 times
with a different amount of heap held before each and takes the floor away. It fails against the
asset (100 of 100 invalid) and passes with the object linked (0 of 100, three runs). The offset,
thick solid, shell, draft, fillet and pipe suites of the package pass with it linked.

Upstream: Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1600, whose first commit is 0053 and whose second is this change,
authored with eliasaronson, who found the case. Reported as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3464.

